# Project Rules (omnix)

## Startup protocol (runs before every response)

Follow `packages/adapters/generic/STARTUP_PROTOCOL.md`:

1. Detect Omnix Runtime markers (`.obsidian-ai-memory/`, `AGENTS.md`, etc.).
2. Identify project type and stack from manifests.
3. Retrieve relevant Obsidian memory (balanced mode by default — see `standards/context-engineering.md`).
4. Auto-route to workflow based on request signals.
5. Activate required agent roles (multi-role for cross-cutting tasks).
6. Emit compact startup block, then work.

> "The user gives a goal. The Omnix Runtime determines workflow, agents, context, checks, and memory updates."

## Memory loop (mandatory)

Before answering or editing, read from `.obsidian-ai-memory/`:
- `02-PROJECTS/project-context.md`
- last 3-5 in `01-SESSIONS/YYYY-MM-DD/`
- `03-ERRORS/error-memory.md`
- `04-DECISIONS/decisions.md`
- `07-LESSONS/lessons-learned.md`

After meaningful work, write a session digest at `01-SESSIONS/YYYY-MM-DD/session-HHMM-cursor.md`.

> Every interaction ends with a digest unless I say otherwise.
> Every fixed error becomes a prevention rule in `03-ERRORS/`.

## Engineering rules (apply universally)

- Follow existing project conventions.
- Never repeat known errors. Check `03-ERRORS/` first.
- Ask before destructive commands.
- Never expose secrets.
- Verify (typecheck/tests/build) before claiming completion.
- Prefer small safe changes.
- Record assumptions and open questions in the digest.

See `packages/core/standards/ai-collaboration.md` and `packages/adapters/generic/AGENTS.md` for the full loop.
